  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Formed from Vte + shimau.\n\nNote that shimau conjugates as a normal godan verb.\n\nVte = -te form verb (死ぬ -> 死んで)",
      "html": "Formed from Vte + shimau.<br/><br/>Note that shimau conjugates as a normal godan verb.<br/><br/>Vte = -te form verb (死ぬ -&gt; 死んで)",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "aa6ec58696411d39e01f44d690b875a01d49b61b570d532a451fbffffed03ee3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Note that the Vte+shimau can be shortened in one of two ways depending on the kana used for the 'te' form verb.\n\ne.g. 死んでしまう → 死んじゃう\n凍えてしまう → 凍えちゃう",
      "html": "Note that the Vte+shimau can be shortened in one of two ways depending on the kana used for the 'te' form verb.<br/><br/>e.g. 死んでしまう → 死んじゃう<br/>凍えてしまう → 凍えちゃう",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "dddc73ed90dd14853cd524719e1b021c9cfe90e59a989784b7d7abef0ca3449c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Not always used in negative nuance.",
      "html": "Not always used in negative nuance.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "3703dda7fc6f6b1b50ccad6aff2a663f9afbae59f3b395f7d83db9e509c9a838",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "this is very good",
      "html": "this is very good",
      "credits_raw": "tarun rana",
      "content_sha256": "3b5930c3dcded94071537b1afcb205779bfab6c900aeebb3012da6e22cf56e78",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Vて+しまうhas two uses. One is, as indicated, to emphasize the completeness or finality of the verb action. The other is to indicate that the occurrence or action denoted by the verb is unfortunate or undesired, e.g., なくなってしまいました ([he or she] sadly died)",
      "html": "Vて+しまうhas two uses. One is, as indicated, to emphasize the completeness or finality of the verb action. The other is to indicate that the occurrence or action denoted by the verb is unfortunate or undesired, e.g., なくなってしまいました ([he or she] sadly died)",
      "credits_raw": "Michael Karlin",
      "content_sha256": "13ab7716f31283e03b338312c35c2b69ad5d02b85d6fd375678c847ea53a5415",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
  ],
